When 5,000 people sign the petition, we will deliver it to the County Assembly. When 20,000 sign, we will take it to the national level. This is how we show that the people of Nairobi County are united in demanding the leadership they deserve.

## What the petition demands

The Bill Llia petition calls for:

- **A community health center in every ward**, fully staffed and stocked with essential medicines
- **A county-wide youth skills training** and enterprise program reaching 500 young people annually
- **Clean water within 500 meters** of every household through borehole rehabilitation and pipeline expansion
- **Transparent governance** through public participation, open county budgets, and regular town hall meetings

## How to sign

Visit the **[petition page](/petition)** on this website, fill in your name, email, and ward, and add a personal message about the change you want to see. Every signature brings us one step closer to the government Nairobi County deserves.

## What happens next

The petition signatures are being collected in real time and stored securely. After the election, a government under Bill Llia will treat this petition as a binding mandate — a directive from the people of Nairobi County on what they expect from their next Governor.

"The petition is not about me," Bill said. "It is about us — the people of Nairobi — standing together and saying: we have waited long enough. The change starts now."

**Already signed?** Share the petition link with your friends, family, and community groups. Forward it in your WhatsApp groups. Post it on your social media. The more voices we amplify, the harder we are to ignore.
